<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gezira</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Al Jazirah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gezira ('island') is the fertile plain between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Blue Nile</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-nile">White Nile</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. It was a heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Funj Sultanate of Sennar</a> from the 16th century. Under Anglo-Egyptian rule the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gezira-scheme">Gezira Scheme</a>, opened in 1925 with the Sennar Dam, made it one of the world's largest irrigated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>-growing areas, and it now forms Al Jazirah state.</p></div>
